  ],
  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "When a bank gives you a loan, it feels like you're the customer. In modern finance, you're closer to the raw material.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "bank",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "bill"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "You're not",
            "the customer."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Your loan is an asset to them, a reliable stream of your future payments, with interest.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "bank",
          "kicker": "the flip",
          "line": "Your debt = their asset",
          "sub": "a stream of your payments"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "To a lender, your debt is simply a promise of future cash.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-debt",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · debt"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Banks don't always keep that loan. They bundle thousands together and sell them on to investors.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "bank",
          "big": "bundled",
          "label": "and sold to investors",
          "props": [
            "bill",
            "loop"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Packaging loans and selling them as securities is called securitization.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-sec",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · securitization"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "They earn on the gap between what they pay for money and what they charge you.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "They earn the gap",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "chartUp"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "That spread even has a name, the net interest margin.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-nim",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · net interest margin"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So your mortgage might now be owned by a pension fund halfway across the world.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "center",
          "art": "globe",
          "line": "Owned far away",
          "props": [
            "globe",
            "bill"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "In a very real sense, you yourself are the yield that they package and sell.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "red",
          "line": "You're the yield",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "loop"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So, who actually owns your loan right now?",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "question",
          "art": "bank",
          "line": "Who owns your loan?",
          "sub": "Comment your guess"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s10"
    }
  ]
